From aaa5eb544b02ace99c9c8fd85d9ba683d948c7ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:52:30 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] App Lock: "Lock App to Screen" exit protection for group
 listening
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New Settings → General → Group & security → "Lock App to Screen" toggle.
  Turning it on or off asks for the owner through Android's BiometricPrompt
  (strong biometric, or the device PIN / pattern / password); a cancelled or
  failed prompt changes nothing.
- While on, the app asks Android to pin it (lock task / screen pinning) on each
  visit. Everything inside the app stays usable with no prompts; Back still
  walks back through screens and is only held at the app's root.
- "🔒 App locked" row and a small lock badge (hidden while the full player is
  open) end the locked session after authentication; the setting stays on and
  re-arms on the next visit.
- The preference is saved separately from the live pinning state, which is read
  from ActivityManager and never persisted, so crashes, reboots or updates can't
  trap the owner. Playback is never touched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
